1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:03,050
A great white shark seized this man around the chest.

2
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:05,540
South Australia, 1963.

3
00:00:05,560 --> 00:00:09,040
A spearfishing championship at Aldinga Beach.

4
00:00:09,490 --> 00:00:12,090
Rodney Fox was hunting fish with a speargun.

5
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:15,460
The jaws closed around him and wouldn't let go.

6
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:17,540
He reached for the shark's eyes.

7
00:00:17,560 --> 00:00:18,540
It released him.

8
00:00:19,110 --> 00:00:21,080
Then it came back and seized his float.

9
00:00:21,660 --> 00:00:23,110
He fought free of the line.

10
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:25,280
He was pulled out, barely alive.

11
00:00:25,890 --> 00:00:26,780
Broken ribs.

12
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:27,920
A punctured lung.

13
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:31,970
It took four hundred and sixty-two stitches to close the wounds.

14
00:00:32,790 --> 00:00:34,980
Fox still wanted to go back in the water.

15
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:36,770
So he built a cage.

16
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:39,160
Steel between him and the jaws.

17
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:43,020
From that cage, Ron Taylor filmed great whites underwater.

18
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:45,460
Some of the first footage of its kind.

19
00:00:46,020 --> 00:00:48,410
He ran cage-diving trips for decades.

20
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:52,380
He co-founded a foundation to study and protect great whites.

21
00:00:53,170 --> 00:00:56,470
The shark that nearly killed him turned him into its defender.
